# Pairs with StaleEpochNeverAppends. The claim's durable entry write is a plain
# write, refused only against the loaded entry. Two overlapping claims write out
# of order, the lower epoch lands last, and after a WAL shard restart the entry
# loads below the epoch the newer claim raised, readmitting the superseded
# activation.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsClaimEntryOverwrite
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim overwrites the durable entry instead of max-merging it
PERTURBS: ClaimWrite

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] > Max2(fence, memFence) \/ AlreadyDurable(a)
    /\ fence' = Max2(fence, epoch[a])
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a plain write, checked against the loaded entry only.
    /\ epoch[a] > memFence
    /\ fence' = epoch[a]
--- END
